      "proposal": {
        "hypothesis": "In ShadeTileC, albedo is constant for a pixel and multiplies every accepted light's channel contribution. Accumulating lightColor*k per channel first, then multiplying each accumulated channel by that pixel's albedo once, is algebraically equivalent and removes two of the six channel multiplies per additional contributing light. This is a contrasting reuse/reassociation trial, not a repeat of the earlier half-vector and light-cache candidates; it retains per-channel light colors and all culling and BRDF calculations. Floating-point order changes, so the controller must check the one-level tolerance, including altered light colors, and measure both 1- and 4-core cases.",
